   "design": "Versioned scripts read the pipeline output directly, produce genotype tables and run the allele frequency, Hardy-Weinberg and linkage calculations, instead of copying tables into spreadsheets and calculating there. A scripted annotation step looks up every variant against fixed releases of the public databases, instead of one-by-one look-ups. The report template fills tables from the script output and the geneticist writes the interpretation. Running and checking pipelines, interpreting, discussing and second review stay with the geneticist. No model computes or interprets results.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Tables were copied into spreadsheets and variants looked up by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Scripted statistics and annotation against fixed database releases.",
   "still_hard": "Unusual study designs with no standard test.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing that a linkage signal is a sample mix-up.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "decide_more_often",
    "what": "Re-analyse every new batch instead of waiting for a full dataset."
   },
   "altitude": "Less copying and calculating by hand; interpretation stays.",
